window.MODELRUN = {"model":"Claude Opus 5.5","date":"26 Sep 2026","setup":"Search step: engine.retrieve(question, 5) (build/model-inputs.mjs) → tests/model-run/input.txt. Answer step: a separate assistant session given only tests/model-run/prompt.txt and input.txt (no expected answers, no other files) → tests/model-run/answers.json. Each quote is checked by demo/assets/eval.js.","answers":[{"id":"f01","kind":"answer","code":"HR-01","version":"4","section":"2.1","page":1,"quote":"Office staff may use flexible start and finish times, provided they are at work during the core hours of 10:00 to 16:00 and their team's phones are covered from 08:30 to 17:00.","answer":"You can start early, but you must be at work until at least 16:00 (core hours 10:00-16:00), so finishing at 15:30 is not allowed, and your team's phones must be covered 08:30-17:00."},{"id":"f02","kind":"answer","code":"HR-01","version":"4","section":"4.4","page":2,"quote":"Between 1 November and 24 December warehouse and transport staff may book no more than 5 days' holiday, because this is our busiest time of year.","answer":"Yes, a week and a half would be too much: warehouse staff can book no more than 5 days' holiday between 1 November and 24 December."},{"id":"f03","kind":"answer","code":"HR-01","version":"4","section":"7.3","page":4,"quote":"If you disagree with a formal decision, you can appeal in writing to the Head of People within 5 working days of receiving the outcome letter. The appeal will be heard by a manager who was not involved in the original decision.","answer":"Appeal in writing to the Head of People within 5 working days of getting the outcome letter; a manager not involved in the original decision will hear it."},{"id":"f04","kind":"answer","code":"HR-01","version":"4","section":"6.3","page":4,"quote":"Smoking and vaping are allowed only in the marked shelters at each depot. They are never allowed inside buildings, in the warehouse, on the loading bays or in any company vehicle, including when you are parked up on a break.","answer":"No, vaping is never allowed in a company vehicle, even when parked up on a break; use the marked shelters at the depot."},{"id":"f05","kind":"answer","code":"HR-05","version":"2","section":"3.2","page":2,"quote":"The Finance team must also be in the office on the last 2 working days of each month for month-end close.","answer":"Yes, as Finance you must be in the office on the last 2 working days of every month for month-end close, as well as on your team's fixed team day."},{"id":"f06","kind":"answer","code":"HR-05","version":"2","section":"4.4","page":2,"quote":"If you leave the company, or your hybrid arrangement ends, return all equipment to the IT Service Desk within 7 days. The IT Service Desk can arrange a courier collection if you cannot bring it in.","answer":"Return all the equipment to the IT Service Desk within 7 days of leaving; they can arrange a courier collection if you can't bring it in."},{"id":"f07","kind":"answer","code":"HR-05","version":"2","section":"5.2","page":3,"quote":"Apply on form HR-HW3 at least 4 weeks before you travel. The request needs the approval of both your line manager and HR.","answer":"Apply on form HR-HW3 at least 4 weeks before you go; both your line manager and HR must approve it."},{"id":"f08","kind":"answer","code":"HR-05","version":"2","section":"2.3","page":1,"quote":"Your manager will give you a written decision within 28 days of receiving your form.","answer":"Your manager should give you a written decision within 28 days of receiving your form."},{"id":"f09","kind":"answer","code":"HSE-04","version":"3","section":"4.1","page":2,"quote":"The following must be reported by phone as soon as it is safe to do so: a death, an injury that needs hospital treatment, a fire, a large spill, a collapse of racking and any collision in which someone is hurt. Phone the Duty Manager at your site and the Health, Safety & Environment Manager on ext. 250.","answer":"Phone the Duty Manager at your site and the Health, Safety & Environment Manager on ext. 250 as soon as it is safe to do so."},{"id":"f10","kind":"answer","code":"HSE-04","version":"3","section":"3.2","page":2,"quote":"Every depot has trained first aiders on every shift. Their names are on the noticeboard next to each first aid kit.","answer":"Check the noticeboard next to any first aid kit; it lists the first aiders, and there is one on every shift."},{"id":"f11","kind":"answer","code":"HSE-04","version":"3","section":"6.2","page":3,"quote":"Line managers complete their investigation within 5 working days.","answer":"Near misses are investigated by the line manager of the area, who should finish within 5 working days."},{"id":"f12","kind":"answer","code":"HSE-04","version":"3","section":"4.4","page":2,"quote":"Line managers must tell the Health, Safety & Environment Manager as soon as an injured person has been off work, or unable to do their normal job, for more than 3 days.","answer":"Yes, because he has been off for more than 3 days you must tell the Health, Safety & Environment Manager now."},{"id":"f13","kind":"answer","code":"IT-01","version":"5","section":"2.3","page":2,"quote":"After 5 wrong password attempts your account is locked for 15 minutes; if you need it sooner, call the IT Service Desk.","answer":"Your account unlocks after 15 minutes; call the IT Service Desk if you need it sooner."},{"id":"f14","kind":"answer","code":"IT-01","version":"5","section":"6.3","page":3,"quote":"Any request to change payment details must be checked by phoning the company on a number we already hold, never a number given in the email. Finance will only make the change after a second person has checked it.","answer":"Yes: check the request by phoning the subcontractor on a number we already hold (not one from the email), and Finance only changes it after a second person has checked."},{"id":"f15","kind":"answer","code":"IT-01","version":"5","section":"2.2","page":1,"quote":"If you do not want the app on your own phone, the IT Service Desk will give you a small hardware security key instead.","answer":"Yes, ask the IT Service Desk for a small hardware security key instead of the app."},{"id":"f16","kind":"answer","code":"IT-01","version":"5","section":"6.4","page":4,"quote":"If you click one, you will be asked to complete a short online refresher within 14 days. The results are used to improve our guidance and not for disciplinary action.","answer":"No, you won't be disciplined; you'll just be asked to do a short online refresher within 14 days."},{"id":"f17","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-02","version":"2","section":"3.4","page":2,"quote":"You need a daily rest of at least 11 hours. It can be reduced to 9 hours no more than 3 times between two weekly rests.","answer":"You need at least 11 hours' daily rest, which can be cut to 9 hours no more than 3 times between two weekly rests."},{"id":"f18","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-02","version":"2","section":"5.3","page":3,"quote":"If a medicine's label or your pharmacist says it may affect your driving, tell your line manager or the Fleet Safety Manager before your next shift. You do not have to say what the condition is.","answer":"Yes, tell your line manager or the Fleet Safety Manager before your next shift; you don't have to say what the condition is."},{"id":"f19","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-02","version":"2","section":"6.3","page":4,"quote":"Congestion charges, clean air zone charges, river crossings and road tolls on company routes are paid by the company through its accounts. Do not pay them yourself unless the Transport Planning Office asks you to, in which case claim them back under FIN-03.","answer":"No, the company pays these charges on company routes; only pay yourself if the Transport Planning Office asks, and then claim it back under FIN-03."},{"id":"f20","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-02","version":"2","section":"3.5","page":2,"quote":"If your card is lost, stolen or not working, tell the Transport Planning Office before you drive and follow their instructions on printouts.","answer":"Tell the Transport Planning Office before you drive and follow their instructions on printouts."},{"id":"f21","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-07","version":"1","section":"7.2","page":4,"quote":"Damaged goods are kept in the marked claims area at the depot for 14 days so that the customer or an insurer can inspect them. After that, the Customer Service Manager decides whether they are returned, sold for salvage or disposed of. Staff must never take damaged goods for their own use.","answer":"The pallet stays in the claims area for 14 days, then the Customer Service Manager decides what happens to it; nobody may take any home."},{"id":"f22","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-07","version":"1","section":"6.2","page":3,"quote":"The Customer Service Manager can offer a goodwill credit of up to £100 per claim. Anything larger needs the Head of Operations.","answer":"The Customer Service Manager can offer up to £100 goodwill per claim; anything more needs the Head of Operations."},{"id":"f23","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-07","version":"1","section":"4.3","page":2,"quote":"We do not pay for:\nindirect losses, such as lost profit, missed sales or penalties the customer pays to their own customers;","answer":"No, missed sales are an indirect loss and we don't pay for them."},{"id":"f24","kind":"answer","code":"OPS-07","version":"1","section":"5.3","page":3,"quote":"We aim to give the customer a written decision within 30 days of receiving the full claim. If we need longer, for example because an insurer is involved, Customer Service updates the customer at least every 10 working days.","answer":"We aim to give a written decision within 30 days of receiving the full claim; if it takes longer, the customer gets an update at least every 10 working days."},{"id":"f25","kind":"answer","code":"FIN-03","version":"3","section":"3.3","page":2,"quote":"If you stay with friends or relatives instead of a hotel, you can claim a flat £25 per night to cover a thank-you gift or a meal for your hosts. No receipt is needed for this amount, but you must give the address on the claim.","answer":"Yes, you can claim a flat £25 per night with no receipt, but you must give your sister's address on the claim."},{"id":"f26","kind":"answer","code":"FIN-03","version":"3","section":"2.2","page":2,"quote":"Flights within the UK are only allowed where the same journey would take more than 4 hours by rail, and they need approval from the Finance Director as well as your line manager.","answer":"Only if the train journey would take more than 4 hours, and you need approval from both the Finance Director and your line manager."},{"id":"f27","kind":"answer","code":"FIN-03","version":"3","section":"5.3","page":3,"quote":"You can add 5p per mile for each colleague you carry on the same business journey.","answer":"Yes, you can add 5p per mile for each colleague, so 10p per mile extra for two."},{"id":"f28","kind":"answer","code":"FIN-03","version":"3","section":"6.3","page":4,"quote":"Claims approved by the 20th of the month are paid with that month's salary. Claims approved after the 20th are paid the following month.","answer":"Because it was approved after the 20th, it will be paid with next month's salary."},{"id":"f29","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"f30","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"f31","kind":"answer","code":"FIN-03","version":"2","section":"4.2","page":2,"quote":"You can claim up to £25 for your evening meal, including soft drinks and service, and the day trip limits in 4.1 apply to lunch.","answer":"Under the old version 2 (replaced on 1 March 2026), you could claim up to £25 for an evening meal."},{"id":"z01","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z02","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z03","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z04","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z05","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z06","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z07","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z08","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."},{"id":"z09","kind":"refuse","answer":"The documents don't cover this."}]};
